# YourPHR — bare metal / VM bootstrap
#
#   cp .env.baremetal.example .env      (in the code checkout; start the server from there)
#
# Only what must be correct BEFORE the app can serve its Admin screen belongs here. Everything
# else has a shipped default (config/app-default-config.json in the checkout) and is changed at
# Admin -> Configuration. See docs/architecture/configuration-system.md and docs/deployment/README.md.
#
# Run the server from the code checkout: the shipped defaults are read from ./config there, as in
# ngdpbase. This file says where the INSTANCE lives; the checkout is the code.

# Where this instance keeps everything it owns and must not lose: the databases, the generated
# session and credential keys, configuration overrides, and backups. Back this directory up.
# The databases default to files inside it (spike.db, records.db).
YOURPHR_FAST_STORAGE=/var/lib/yourphr

# Where the compiled Angular app lives: the checkout's dist/web after
# `cd frontend && yarn build -- -c prod`. WITHOUT THIS the server starts, the API answers, and no page
# is served.
YOURPHR_WEB_STATIC_DIR=/opt/yourphr/dist/web

# Encryption keys: both required, both supplied by you (yourphr#796).
#   generate each with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Keep a copy OFF this machine: the backup key is the only thing a restore needs.
# An instance that starts without a database key creates an UNENCRYPTED database.
YOURPHR_DATABASE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
YOURPHR_BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Optional: only if 8080 is taken, or a reverse proxy expects otherwise.
# YOURPHR_WEB_LISTEN_PORT=8080
